+#pragma once
+
+// nvme-direct-expert-tier (0.5.3 LISBON), design note D2/D3 -- the production
+// arcwell transport for the load-time pinned fill.
+//
+// `pinned_nvme_fill.hpp` (patch 0048) carries the schedule only; its Transport
+// interface is injected. This header supplies the production implementation:
+//
+//   1. ONE xe VRAM BO per (MoE layer, tensor), 64 KiB-rounded, created with the
+//      raw DRM ioctls exactly as arcwell's own stub/test/aw_expert_test.c and
+//      tools/arcwell_cl_slot_proof.c do (DRM_IOCTL_XE_GEM_CREATE with VRAM
+//      placement + NEEDS_VISIBLE_VRAM + CPU_CACHING_WC, then
+//      DRM_IOCTL_PRIME_HANDLE_TO_FD).
+//   2. AW_IOC_MAP_BUFFER registration, asserting AW_MAP_F_REQUIRE_P2P. A
+//      system-memory BO is refused by the module (-ERANGE); there is no
+//      host-bounce fallback.
+//   3. AW_IOC_SUBMIT_BATCH / AW_IOC_BATCH_WAIT driving, four batches in flight
+//      (the Scheduler owns the depth), with out_submitted/out_err checked --
+//      the ioctl return alone is not enough (observed: an unaligned geometry
+//      returns 0 with submitted=0, err=-22).
+//   4. Correct lifetime: the BO's GEM handle is owned by the render-node fd;
+//      the exported dma-buf is a separate reference; arcwell takes its own
+//      dma_buf_get, so the caller may close the exported fd after a successful
+//      map; a registration is released by AW_IOC_UNMAP_BUFFER or fd close, and
+//      in-flight batches hold the buffer until collected.
+//
+// GEOMETRY. The plugin's device layout is three per-tensor slot regions per
+// layer (the fused GEMV kernel indexes each by `expert_id * per_tensor_bytes`,
+// moe_3gemm_swiglu_mlp.cl). The ext4 store's record is `gate|up|down`
+// concatenated for one expert, so ONE expert becomes THREE page-aligned
+// requests (each `per_tensor_bytes` = 200 pages at the served shape), not one
+// -- a dated correction to the design note's "one expert = one request", which
+// held only for the synthetic store whose whole file mapped to one
+// destination. The store ordinal is layer-major (verified 0 mismatches against
+// the store manifest): ordinal = dense_layer_index * capacity + slot, file
+// `expert_%04u.bin`. FIEMAP runs once per file and the absolute LBA is
+// `fe_physical/512 + partition_start` (docs/USING_ARCWELL.md section 5).
+
